{"pdf_page": 356, "book_page": 347, "items": [{"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [46.7, 713.0, 63.4, 704.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [46.6, 566.3, 63.6, 557.2]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [46.5, 370.6, 63.3, 361.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "In each case, work out the M, by adding up the relative atomic masses (A, values), and then attach the unit \"g\" to give the mass of 1 mole.", "bbox": [66.8, 714.4, 300.7, 680.5]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "a 27g", "bbox": [67.2, 681.6, 100.6, 668.3]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "c 4.30× 16= 68.8g", "bbox": [67.5, 659.6, 155.8, 647.0]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "b 331g", "bbox": [67.2, 670.8, 105.1, 657.5]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "d 0.70× 62 = 43.4g", "bbox": [67.5, 648.8, 155.5, 636.2]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "0.015× 85=1.275g", "bbox": [76.9, 637.6, 165.2, 625.0]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "× 286 = 68.64g Don't forget the water of crystallisation", "bbox": [78.7, 626.1, 266.3, 603.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "Strictly speaking the answers to d), e) and f) shouldn't be quoted to more than 2 significant figures, because the number of moles is only quoted to that precision.)", "bbox": [79.4, 602.7, 299.3, 568.2]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "In each case, work out the mass of 1 mole as above, and then work out how many moles you've got in the stated mass. You can use the equation:", "bbox": [66.8, 566.4, 299.0, 532.9]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.8, 646.4, 75.1, 638.2]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.9, 635.1, 74.7, 627.4]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.6, 625.3, 73.8, 617.0]}, {"label": "text", "text": "number of moles =", "bbox": [66.8, 527.7, 148.2, 515.5]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.5, 506.4, 75.2, 498.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.6, 485.0, 75.4, 476.3]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.0, 461.7, 75.3, 453.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.5, 439.7, 75.5, 430.3]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.5, 415.5, 75.0, 407.8]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [68.1, 391.2, 73.7, 381.6]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [68.2, 351.7, 75.4, 342.4]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.6, 327.0, 75.0, 319.3]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [67.2, 308.3, 75.0, 300.2]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [68.0, 289.1, 74.7, 281.3]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [68.2, 268.9, 73.9, 260.6]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [47.0, 248.8, 75.0, 239.3]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "20 40 = 0.5mol", "bbox": [79.7, 513.7, 133.6, 491.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "3.20", "bbox": [79.4, 490.7, 101.2, 479.2]}, {"label": "text", "text": "mass of 1 mole", "bbox": [146.1, 521.4, 210.7, 508.8]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "=0.0200mol 160", "bbox": [81.1, 486.2, 155.8, 468.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "2000 = 25.2 mol; Don't forget to convert kg to g! 79.5", "bbox": [79.7, 467.7, 276.4, 445.3]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "50", "bbox": [85.6, 444.6, 100.2, 433.5]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "= 0.2mol 249.5", "bbox": [79.4, 440.4, 145.7, 422.3]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "1000000 = 17900 mol (or 17857, although this is precise 56 to more significant figures than the A,).", "bbox": [80.0, 421.9, 302.8, 394.4]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "= 5.0 × 10-4 mol (0.0005 mol) 64", "bbox": [79.4, 396.1, 227.4, 373.1]}, {"label": "text", "text": "4× 58.5=234g", "bbox": [76.9, 371.0, 147.5, 359.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "37 =0.5mol 74", "bbox": [79.4, 356.7, 133.6, 334.7]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "1000 =25mol 40", "bbox": [80.0, 334.0, 140.9, 311.3]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "× 79.5 = 9.94g (9.9375g)", "bbox": [78.0, 309.9, 208.3, 297.4]}, {"label": "text", "text": "4", "bbox": [83.2, 295.6, 93.6, 284.8]}, {"label": "text", "text": "0.1", "bbox": [79.7, 284.5, 95.7, 273.6]}, {"label": "text", "text": "=40g", "bbox": [93.6, 293.5, 124.2, 276.8]}, {"label": "text", "text": "1", "bbox": [93.3, 274.3, 101.6, 263.9]}, {"label": "text", "text": "0.004g", "bbox": [79.4, 265.3, 112.7, 250.6]}, {"label": "text", "text": "=250g", "bbox": [113.1, 271.2, 147.5, 256.5]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [74.0, 248.3, 293.7, 175.8]}, {"label": "table", "text": "|                       | P             | H             |\n|-----------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Combining mass        | 9.39g         | 0.61g         |\n| No. of moles of atoms | 9.39 =0.30 31 | 0.61 = 0.61 1 |\n| Ratio of moles        | 1             | 2             |", "bbox": [74.0, 248.3, 293.7, 175.8]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Empirical formula is PH_2", "bbox": [79.7, 174.5, 180.5, 162.0]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [68.7, 158.7, 305.9, 53.3]}, {"label": "table", "text": "|                       | K             | N             | o             |\n|-----------------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Combining mass        | 5.85g         | 2.10g         | 4.80g         |\n| No. of moles of atoms | 5.85 =0.15 39 | 2.10 =0.15 14 | 4.80 = 0.3 16 |\n| Ratio of moles        | 1             | 1             | 2             |", "bbox": [68.7, 158.7, 305.9, 53.3]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Empirical formula is KNO2", "bbox": [80.0, 52.1, 187.8, 39.5]}, {"label": "text", "text": "mass Empirical formula is Na2S2O_3}", "bbox": [166.2, 530.8, 191.2, 520.7]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [323.7, 403.6, 339.5, 393.8]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [346.2, 712.6, 580.5, 574.2]}, {"label": "table", "text": "|                                            | Na                | S             | o             |\n|--------------------------------------------|-------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Combining mass                             | 3.22g             | 4.48g         | 3.36g         |\n| No. of moles of atoms                      | 3.22 =0.14 23     | 4.48 =0.14 32 | 3.36 =0.21 16 |\n| Ratio of moles (divide by smallest number) | 1 simplifies to 2 | 1 2           | 1.5 3         |", "bbox": [346.2, 712.6, 580.5, 574.2]}, {"label": "table", "text": "|                                            | Carbon         | Hydrogen    | Bromine         |\n|--------------------------------------------|----------------|-------------|-----------------|\n| Given %                                    | 22.0           | 4.6         | 73.4            |\n| No. of moles of atoms                      | 22.0 =1.833 12 | 4.6 = 4.6 1 | 73.4 =0.9175 80 |\n| Ratio of moles (divide by smallest number) | 2              | 5           | 1               |", "bbox": [349.0, 558.4, 582.7, 421.2]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Empirical formula is C2HgBr", "bbox": [356.5, 419.6, 470.1, 407.1]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "848 The mass of oxygen is 2.84–1.24 = 1.60g", "bbox": [324.1, 405.0, 527.8, 391.1]}, {"label": "table", "text": "|                       | P              | o             |\n|-----------------------|----------------|---------------|\n| Combining mass        | 1.24g          | 1.60g         |\n| No. of moles of atoms | 1.24 = 0.04 31 | 1.60 =0.10 16 |\n| Ratio of moles        | 1              | 2.5           |", "bbox": [357.0, 389.8, 570.4, 318.1]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Whole numbers must be used, therefore multiply by 2 to get the empirical formula P2O_5.", "bbox": [355.8, 317.2, 575.2, 292.1]}, {"label": "formula", "text": "\\frac { 2 8 4 } { 1 4 2 } = 2", "bbox": [389.6, 279.9, 426.1, 256.9]}, {"label": "list_item", "text": "bP_2}O5 has an M, of 142", "bbox": [344.2, 292.5, 448.6, 279.6]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Therefore there must be two lots of the empirical formula in a molecule.", "bbox": [355.8, 257.3, 555.2, 233.9]}, {"label": "text", "text": "Molecular formula is P4O10", "bbox": [356.1, 232.2, 466.9, 219.3]}, {"label": "table", "text": "Empirical formula is C4H8O\n\n|                                            | Carbon         | Hydrogen     | Oxygen          |\n|--------------------------------------------|----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| Given %                                    | 66.7           | 11.1         | 22.2            |\n| Combining mass in 100g                     | 66.7g          | 11.1g        | 22.2g           |\n| No. of moles of atoms                      | 66.7 =5.558 12 | 11.1 =11.1 1 | 22.2 =1.3875 16 |\n| Ratio of moles (divide by smallest number) | 4              | 8            | 1               |", "bbox": [354.2, 215.2, 585.9, 53.3]}, {"label": "caption", "text": "Empirical formula is C4H8O", "bbox": [356.8, 52.0, 468.0, 39.5]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [345.3, 559.2, 352.5, 550.6]}, {"label": "text", "text": "p", "bbox": [345.2, 559.7, 353.7, 549.6]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [344.9, 291.4, 352.4, 282.2]}, {"label": "picture", "text": "", "bbox": [323.8, 216.4, 352.0, 206.9]}]}